# [DD-13b.W1.3] A FLAT IMPORT LANDING ON A GROUP THE CALLER ALREADY HAS.
#
# `(?&*=name)` puts the exports in the CALLER's own scope, which is the whole
# point of the form — a flat row is counted by `nnames` and found by
# `match_api.md` §6's bsearch, indistinguishable from a group the caller
# declared. That is exactly why the clash must refuse: two rows sharing one
# name would make that bsearch return whichever the sort happened to put
# first.
target = t

pattern ^(?<kept>z)(?&*=piece)$
name t

pattern (?<kept>a)
name piece
export kept
